// Rimmington and the other loc_97xx mine rocks (Corey, 2026-09-07).
//
// "Rimmington mine - rocks when mined use lime rock."
//
// Moved out of content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.loc; a loc cannot be redeclared while it still
// exists there ("Duplicate config found"), so the whole contiguous 9708-9725 run comes along.
// Nothing below is invented - every line is the cache's own, with category= and param= corrected.
//
// What was wrong. These fifteen rocks are a clean 3-models x 5-ores grid:
//
//                model=loc_4027   model=loc_4028   model=loc_2110
//   copper         9708             9709             9710
//   clay           9711             9712             9713
//   tin            9714             9715             9716
//   iron           9717             9718             9719
//   gold           9720             9721             9722
//
// (the ore is recol2d: 26981 copper, 22025 clay, 14798 tin, 6242 iron, 31393 gold.)
//
// Every loc_4027-modelled and loc_4028-modelled rock had
//
//     param=next_loc_stage_mining,loc_4027   (or loc_4028)
//
// pointing at itself - at the plain scenery loc whose own name is "Pile of Rock" and whose examine
// text is literally "A pile of lime rock". So mining a copper rock at Rimmington turned it into a
// pile of lime rock, and because loc_4027/loc_4028 carry no category=mining_rock_normal and no
// param=mining_rock_empty,1, mining.rs2's loc_param(mining_rock_empty) check could not even
// recognise it as a spent rock afterwards.
//
// The five loc_2110-modelled rocks pointed at rocks1 instead, with a "//TODO this is wrong but it
// doesn't accept loc_2110" beside each one. rocks1 at least behaves (it is a proper empty rock)
// but it is the wrong model and it examines as "Stoney!".
//
// What it should point at. The cache already contains the depleted variants and nothing in the
// codebase referenced any of them: loc_9723, loc_9724 and loc_9725, all named "Rocks", all
// examining as "A rocky outcrop.", and - the giveaway - all three carrying recol1 but NO recol2.
// Every live rock above has recol2s=6342 plus an ore-coloured recol2d; a rock with no ore colour
// is a rock with no ore in it. They are matched to the three models by the copper row, which is
// the row Jagex authored them from: 9708/9709/9710 carry mapscene 24/25/12 and 9723/9724/9725
// carry mapscene 24/25/12 in the same order.
//
// The one cosmetic compromise: there are three depleted variants for five ore rows, so a depleted
// gold rock inherits the copper row's mapscene. 12, 24 and 25 are all rock icons and the
// difference is a couple of pixels on the minimap.
//
// Also fixed here: loc_9712 (clay) and loc_9721 (gold) shipped with no category= at all, so both
// were completely inert - the Mine option did nothing. They are wired up the same as their
// siblings, and added to the clay and gold tables in mine.dbrow.

[loc_9708]
name=Rocks
desc=A rocky outcrop.
model=loc_4027
recol1s=15854
recol1d=12480
recol2s=6342
recol2d=26981
op1=Mine
op2=Prospect
op3=hidden
mapscene=24
blockrange=no
ambient=10
category=mining_rock_normal
param=next_loc_stage_mining,loc_9723

